# Case: Offline received history must not auto-apply on Desktop startup
# Mode: native
# Environment: disposable-guest
# Purpose: Separate persistent offline history from fresh native clipboard delivery.
# Steps:
#   Pair an owned peer; quit Desktop; run the same profile as a standalone service; receive text; reopen normal Desktop; then deliver fresh text.
# Expected:
#   The standalone service receives history without touching the clipboard; Desktop replaces it, retains history and preserves the existing clipboard baseline; fresh text subsequently applies without echo.
# Forbidden:
#   Old backlog auto-application, an uninitialized profile, discarded history, parallel clipboard owners or host clipboard access.

system-board-write 'UNIC-D offline startup baseline'
start
ui-click listItem 设置…
ui-wait listItem 同步
ui-click listItem 同步
ui-enabled switch 启用同步
ui-click switch 启用同步
config-equals sync.enabled true
connect-policy-peer
screenshot before-offline-service
system-offline-backlog
screenshot reopened-after-offline-backlog
